## Notification Protocol

### When to Post a Notification

Post a notification when your changes might affect other sessions:

| Change Type | Notify? | Priority |
|-------------|---------|----------|
| Template structure change | Yes - ALL | High |
| Shared file renamed/moved | Yes - affected | High |
| API/interface change | Yes - consumers | High |
| New convention established | Yes - ALL | Medium |
| Bug fix in shared code | Yes - users | Medium |
| Documentation update | Optional | Low |
| Internal refactor (no API change) | No | - |

### Notification Template

```markdown
### NOTIF-[NUMBER]

**Timestamp:** [YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM]
**From Session:** [Project Name - Session ID]
**To Session:** [Target or "ALL"]
**Priority:** High | Medium | Low
**Subject:** [Brief description]

**Message:**
[What changed, why, and what receivers need to know]

**Files Affected:**
- [list files]

**Action Required:**
- [ ] [what receiver must do]

**Acknowledged By:**
```

### Acknowledgment Protocol

When you receive a notification addressed to your session:

1. **Read** the full notification
2. **Complete** all required actions
3. **Add acknowledgment** with your session ID and timestamp
4. **Move** the notification to "Acknowledged Notifications" section

### Priority Definitions

| Priority | Meaning | Response Time |
|----------|---------|---------------|
| **High** | Breaking change, must act before continuing | Immediate |
| **Medium** | Important change, act soon | Before next work package |
| **Low** | FYI, acknowledge when convenient | End of session |

---

## Session ID Format

Session IDs follow the pattern: `[PROJECT]-[DATE]-[SEQUENCE]`

Examples:
- `CxMS-2026-01-20-A` (first CxMS session on Jan 20)
- `LPR-2026-01-20-B` (second LPR session on Jan 20)
- `ASB-2026-01-21-A` (first ASB session on Jan 21)

